// The world the `andy` sample builds against.
//
// Like ferris and keith, it exports nothing but the player data plane. Andy is
// written in C# and compiled to a WASI 0.2.3 reactor component with
// componentize-dotnet (NativeAOT-LLVM + WASI SDK). The .NET runtime lowers the
// BCL onto the WASI 0.2 imports automatically:
//
//   * Console.WriteLine        -> wasi:cli/stdout (Andy's gentle hedgehog banter)
//   * System.IO.File           -> wasi:filesystem (his little friend-book)
//   * DateTime / Environment    -> wasi:clocks, wasi:cli/environment
//
// So those imports don't need to be declared here — NativeAOT-LLVM contributes
// the WASI import world and the component encoder merges it with the `player`
// export world emitted by `wit-bindgen c-sharp`. Keeping the bindgen world to
// just the interface we implement mirrors how ferris and keith build.
package better-together:andy@0.1.0;

/// A single Andy player component: a WASI 0.2.3 reactor that exports the
/// Better Together player interface.
world andy {
    export better-together:gardener/player@0.1.0;
}
